530 : (e) [-The General Partner shall not be required to excuse or exclude a Limited Partner from an Investment based solely on such Limited Partner's internal investment policies, guidelines, or preferences, unless such policies or guidelines reflect binding legal or regulatory requirements applicable to such Limited Partner. For the avoidance of doubt, an investment restriction adopted as a matter of internal policy by a Limited Partner, such as an environmental, social, or governance policy or a sector-exclusion list, shall not constitute a legal or regulatory requirement for purposes of this Section 3.6 unless such restriction is mandated by a law, statute, regulation, or court order binding upon such Limited Partner.-] {+The General Partner shall excuse a Limited Partner from any Investment that is inconsistent with such Limited Partner's published investment policy statement or guidelines adopted by its governing board, provided that such Limited Partner has delivered a copy of the applicable investment policy statement or guidelines to the General Partner within thirty (30) days of the date of this Agreement. For the avoidance of doubt, the General Partner shall excuse Meridian State Teachers' Retirement System from any Investment in companies the primary business of which involves the manufacturing, distribution, or sale of tobacco products, civilian firearms and ammunition, thermal coal extraction, or the ownership or operation of private prison or detention facilities.+}
